<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 2" layout="Heading 2">Example 2: the variational 1-form as a conservation law of T[1]E</Text-field></Title>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L6" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal"># omega'_psi from Example 2, with q -&gt; Cartan forms.
psi1x  := TotalDiff(psi1, [2]):  psi1xx := TotalDiff(psi1, [2,2]):
omega1 := evalDG(  psi1  * Cu1[]    &amp;wedge Dx &amp;wedge Dy
   - psi1xx* Cu1[]    &amp;wedge Dt &amp;wedge Dx
   + (2*u1[2]*psi1 + psi1xx) * Cu1[] &amp;wedge Dt &amp;wedge Dy
   + psi1  * Cu1[2,2] &amp;wedge Dt &amp;wedge Dy
   - psi1x * Cu1[2]   &amp;wedge Dt &amp;wedge Dy
   + psi1  * Cu1[2,3] &amp;wedge Dt &amp;wedge Dy
   - psi1x * Cu1[3]   &amp;wedge Dt &amp;wedge Dy ):</Text-field>
</Input>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L7" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal"># CHECK 2 (expect 0): the off-shell identity (3.1) with chi = q, i.e.
#   d_0(omega'_psi) = psi l_F(q) - l*_F(psi) q  (eq. (3.7) and Section 3.2).
# With q written as the Cartan form theta the right-hand side acquires the
# factor (-1)^p = -1 (p = 1), see Section 4 and Appendix A; hence sgn = 1 below.
sgn := 1:
dvF := VerticalExteriorDerivative(F_form1):
evalDG( HorizontalExteriorDerivative(omega1)
   + sgn*( psi1*(dvF &amp;wedge Vol) - AdjLinF(psi1)*(Cu1[] &amp;wedge Vol) ) );</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display=""></Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
</Section>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 2" layout="Heading 2">Example 3: the presymplectic operator D_x</Text-field></Title>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L8" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal"># Example 3, eq. (3.8): CHECK 3 (expect 0): l*_E o Dx - (Dx)* o l_E = 0 on E, i.e.
# l*_F(Dx chi) + Dx(l_F(chi)) vanishes on E for symbolic chi = v1.
E_v := Prolong( evalDG(v1[]*D_u1[]), K ):
lFv := LieDerivative(E_v, F_form1):
OnShell( AdjLinF(TotalDiff(v1[], [2])) + TotalDiff(lFv, [2]) );</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFEiMEYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdub3JtYWxGJw==">IiIh</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
</Section>
<Section collapsed="false" isCollapsible="true" drawButton="true" MultipleChoiceAnswerIndex="-1" MultipleChoiceRandomizeChoices="false" TrueFalseAnswerIndex="-1" EssayAnswerRows="5" EssayAnswerColumns="60"><Title><Text-field style="Heading 2" layout="Heading 2">Example 4: Lagrangian and the scaling origin</Text-field></Title>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L9" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal"># Example 4, eq. (3.17) and Remark 6: nabla_e*(F) = E(L) for nabla_e = D_x, i.e.
# CHECK 4 (expect 0): E(lambda) + D_x(F) = 0 (Section 8.2).
lambda := (u1[1]*u1[2] + u1[2,2]*(u1[2,2] + u1[2,3]))/2 - u1[2]^3/3:
EL := EulerLagrange(lambda):
simplify( EL[1] + TotalDiff(F_form1, [2]) );</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFEiMEYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdub3JtYWxGJw==">IiIh</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L10" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal"># Scaling symmetry -3t dt - x dx - y dy + u du (Example 4, Section 8.2):
# characteristic phi_s = u + 3t u_t + x u_x + y u_y on the ambient jet space.
phis_ambient := u1[] + 3*t*u1[1] + x*u1[2] + y*u1[3]:
phis := OnShell(phis_ambient):     # the same characteristic in internal coordinates
# CHECK 5 (expect 0): phi_s is a symmetry.
E_phis := Prolong( evalDG(phis*D_u1[]), K ):
OnShell( LieDerivative(E_phis, F_form1) );</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFEiMEYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdub3JtYWxGJw==">IiIh</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
<Group hide-input="false" labelreference="L11" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field prompt="&gt; " style="Maple Input" layout="Normal"># CHECK 6 (expect 0): the cosymmetry (3.5) originates from the scaling, eq. (8.3):
# D_x(phi_s) = psi identically on the ambient jet space (no restriction to E).
expand( TotalDiff(phis_ambient, [2]) - psi1 );</Text-field>
</Input>
<Output><Text-field style="2D Output" layout="Maple Output"><Equation executable="false" style="2D Output" display="LUkjbW5HNiMvSSttb2R1bGVuYW1lRzYiSSxUeXBlc2V0dGluZ0dJKF9zeXNsaWJHRic2JFEiMEYnLyUsbWF0aHZhcmlhbnRHUSdub3JtYWxGJw==">IiIh</Equation></Text-field>
</Output>
</Group>
